{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Consult on new Commons\u2019 seat colours for Parliament\u2019s refurbishment",
        "additional_details": "Whilst green morocco leather benches have been the standard for over 300 years, modernising our political spaces could visually signal a more transparent era. A public consultation could give citizens a direct stake in how the home of British democracy looks and feels. This petition does not demand any specific outcome, nor does it ask for immediate structural changes. Instead, it requests that Parliament provides the public with the opportunity to choose the colour scheme when it comes to Parliament\u2019s Restoration and Renewal scheme decisions.",
        "background": "I believe the refurbishment of Parliament is a historic chance to update the Palace of Westminster. Instead of keeping the traditional green benches, I want a public consultation on a new bench colour scheme, to modernise the Commons and make it look like a truly 21st-century social democracy.",
